  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 104413,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.Reachy",
  "published": "2026-09-16T15:35:59.18Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0-preview.2 - the robot's own audio, both directions, verified on hardware. ReachySpeaker plays synthesised speech out of the robot's speaker, converting to the 16 kHz mono 16-bit WAV the daemon requires (it does not transcode, and the symptom of getting it wrong is silence or wrong-speed audio rather than an error); playback is daemon-side on the daemon's clock, so speech and motion do not drift apart over a wireless link. PlayTestToneAsync proves that path with no model in the way - reaching it through a real reply costs a language model and a cold voice load, and a failure anywhere in that chain looks identical to broken audio. ReachyEars exposes the robot's four-microphone array as a MediaStream for speech recognition; note that the SDK's own micStream is the OUTBOUND direction and defaults to a silent placeholder, and that the robot's media event fires once during the connect handshake - so the subscription must exist before connecting. VerifyHeadMatrixConventionAsync now homes first and samples a window, instead of taking one reading mid-travel and reporting a different layout each run.",
